 # Changelog
 All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 
+## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-12
+
+AI-DLC 1.0.0 is 2.10.0 plus a `harness` distribution that runs the whole workflow inside Coding Harness (1.1.0 or newer). It is a fork release: its version is independent of upstream's, so installs turn the update check off. **Install:** `aidlc config --harness harness` in a project, then `/aidlc` in a harness session.
+
+* `aidlc version` reports `1.0.0`; `aidlc config --harness harness` and `aidlc doctor` support Coding Harness alongside the seven existing distributions, and a project can carry it together with Claude Code.
+* The harness distribution runs the engine's hooks through an in-process adapter, injects the method tree, and keeps the Claude Code distribution's fidelity: structured questions and approval gates through `ask`, stage rule bundles for every dispatch, plan approval, reviewer scope, sensors and usage accounting.
+* Reviewers run on a model family other than the builder's, the developer agent carries a continuous advisor that reviews against the human-approved artifacts, and AI-DLC contracts (no stubs, engine-owned state files, read-only reviewers, evidence before "done") are enforced as stream-time rules.
+* Compaction summaries are built from the workflow record, and a turn that crosses a stage boundary compacts once context use passes `harness.compactAtStageBoundary`.
+* A new `project-checks` sensor (every distribution) runs the project's own lint, type-check and test commands from `aidlc/spaces/<space>/checkers.json` on each source file Code Generation and Build and Test write; on Coding Harness, `/aidlc-checkers` discovers them.
+* On Coding Harness the developer agent hands off to the `smol` model role at its first edit (prewalk), and a bugfix observes the defect under the debugger before its first source edit.
+* Python bytecode caches (`__pycache__`) are no longer counted as application source. A stage that ran Python tests could not complete, because the bytecode showed up as unclaimed source changes and a manifest claim on a Git-ignored path was refused. Source fingerprints recorded with a `__pycache__` present change once, so an in-flight Construction review may need one fresh pass after the upgrade.
+
 ## [2.10.0] - 2026-09-24
 
 AI-DLC 2.10.0 rolls up the user-visible changes merged since 2.9.0, including conversation-aware AIDA review workflows, stronger human authority and recovery across Construction, multi-harness project coexistence, and reliability corrections across providers, worktrees, hooks, sensors, and stage routing. **Upgrade:** run `aidlc update`, then run `aidlc config --yes` in each project to refresh its harness runtime. Manual-copy users must replace the complete `runtime/<harness>/` tree from `aidlc-copy-runtime-2.10.0.tar.gz`.
